# You design and build LEGO Technic models one step at a time, in a build language.
#
# For each step you write:
# ADD name partnumber color
# CONNECT part.point -> part.point LOCKED|TURNS|STIFF   (points: hole1.., axlehole1.., pin1.., axle1.., clip1..; LOCKED = cross in cross, turn together; TURNS = free; STIFF = friction pin)
# Optional: MESH a.teeth b.teeth / RATIO a b x/y / GROUP g (opens a side build) / END (closes it) / ATTACH g (joins a finished side build into the main model)
# WHY one plain sentence: what this step builds and what it is for.
# A point ending in ~ is an estimate; ? means not known.
#
# Rules: only use real points of each part; a round pin never goes in a cross hole; a shaft that must turn needs round holes; a worm needs stops on both sides; gears must sit at the right distance.
STEP 1
ADD rail1 14720 ltbluegray
ADD pin1 2780 black
ADD gear161 94925 ltbluegray
ADD hub21 87082 ltbluegray
ADD axle61 3706 black
CONNECT pin1.pin1 -> rail1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT hub21.pin1 -> rail1.hole2~ STIFF
WHY Starts the first long side rail with a friction hub pinned to each end post for a shaft to ride in.

STEP 2
ADD bevel1 32270 black
ADD axle31 4519 ltbluegray
ADD axle81 3707 black
CONNECT bevel1.axlehole1 -> axle61.axle1 LOCKED
WHY Builds the first gear pair on its own axle so the two gears turn together.

STEP 3
ADD bush1 6538c darkbluegray
CONNECT bush1.? -> axle81.axle1~ TURNS
WHY Threads a spacer bush onto the shaft so the next gear sits clear of its neighbour.

STEP 4
ADD hub41 55615 ltbluegray
ADD pin2 2780 black
ADD gear162 94925 ltbluegray
CONNECT hub41.pin1 -> hub21.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin2.pin1 -> hub41.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT gear162.axlehole1 -> axle81.axle2 LOCKED
WHY Pins a four-way hub to the rail and adds the next gear of the stack.

STEP 5
ADD axle121 3708 black
WHY Runs the long axle through the gear row so it can carry more gears further down.

STEP 6
ADD stub41 87083 darkbluegray
ADD plate1 60483 darkbluegray
WHY Adds a stub axle through a small brace plate to hold the next shaft square.

STEP 7
ADD pin3 2780 black
ADD hub11 15100 black
ADD ring1 18947 darkbluegray
ADD gear163 94925 ltbluegray
ADD gear81 10928 darkbluegray
ADD axle51 32073 ltbluegray
CONNECT pin3.pin1 -> plate1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT hub11.pin1 -> plate1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT ring1.? -> stub41.axle1~ TURNS
CONNECT gear163.axlehole1 -> stub41.axle2 LOCKED
CONNECT gear81.axlehole1 -> stub41.axle3 LOCKED
WHY Builds a second gear shaft with a spacer bush, pins it to the rail, and hangs a single-pin hub, an unlabeled driving ring and a reinforced 8-tooth gear on the cluster.

STEP 8
ADD crown1 3648 darkbluegray
ADD axle71 44294 ltbluegray
ADD pin4 2780 black
ADD plate2 60483 darkbluegray
ADD gear164 94925 ltbluegray
ADD pin5 2780 black
ADD hub42 55615 ltbluegray
ADD plate3 60483 darkbluegray
CONNECT crown1.? -> axle51.axle1~ TURNS
CONNECT pin4.pin1 -> hub11.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT gear164.axlehole1 -> axle71.axle1 LOCKED
CONNECT pin5.pin1 -> plate2.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT hub42.pin1 -> plate2.hole1~ STIFF
WHY Finishes the first cluster: a crown gear, a stop axle, more pins and plates, a gear and a four-way hub close off the shaft row.

STEP 9
ADD pin6 2780 black
CONNECT pin6.pin1 -> plate3.hole1~ STIFF
WHY Important: starts the second box frame - its open window must face the gear stack already built, or the shafts won't clear it.

STEP 10
ADD frame1 64179 ltbluegray
ADD gear165 94925 ltbluegray
ADD bush2 6538c darkbluegray
CONNECT gear165.axlehole1 -> axle71.axle2 LOCKED
CONNECT bush2.? -> axle71.axle3~ TURNS
WHY Fits the main side frame onto the rail assembly and builds another gear and spacer bush into it.

STEP 11
ADD pin7 2780 black
ADD plate4 60483 darkbluegray
ADD hub43 55615 ltbluegray
CONNECT pin7.pin1 -> frame1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT hub43.pin1 -> plate4.hole1~ STIFF
WHY Pins the frame, adds a brace plate and a four-way hub to carry the next shaft.

STEP 12
ADD pin8 2780 black
CONNECT pin8.pin1 -> hub43.hole1~ STIFF
WHY Pins the frame near the gear row to keep it from sliding sideways.

STEP 13
ADD gear166 94925 ltbluegray
CONNECT gear166.axlehole1 -> axle71.axle4 LOCKED
WHY Adds one more gear to the stack.

STEP 14
WHY Important: flip the sub-assembly here - the remaining pins go in from the face shown on the next page.

STEP 15
ADD pin9 2780 black
ADD plate5 60483 darkbluegray
CONNECT pin9.pin1 -> hub43.hole2~ STIFF
WHY Pins the frame and braces it with a plate.

STEP 16
ADD hub44 55615 ltbluegray
ADD pin10 2780 black
CONNECT hub44.pin1 -> plate5.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin10.pin1 -> hub44.hole1~ STIFF
WHY Adds a four-way hub and a pin to carry the next stub shaft.

STEP 17
ADD topbeam1 41239 ltbluegray
WHY Lays the long 13-hole beam across the top of both frames to tie the whole gearbox box together.

STEP 18
ADD gear167 94925 ltbluegray
ADD pin11 2780 black
CONNECT gear167.axlehole1 -> axle71.axle5 LOCKED
CONNECT pin11.pin1 -> topbeam1.hole1~ STIFF
WHY Adds a gear and pins it in place on the long axle.

STEP 19
ADD rail2 14720 ltbluegray
ADD pin12 2780 black
CONNECT pin12.pin1 -> rail2.hole1~ STIFF
WHY Adds the second long rail and a pin to start closing the far side of the box.

STEP 20
ADD gear168 94925 ltbluegray
CONNECT gear168.axlehole1 -> axle71.axle6 LOCKED
WHY Adds one more gear to the long axle.

STEP 21
ADD hub22 87082 ltbluegray
ADD axle62 3706 black
CONNECT hub22.pin1 -> rail2.hole2~ STIFF
WHY Connects a hub coupler and locks the next axle into the frame.

STEP 22
ADD bevel2 32270 black
ADD axle32 4519 ltbluegray
CONNECT bevel2.axlehole1 -> axle62.axle1 LOCKED
WHY Locks a double-bevel gear and a short axle onto the stepper cluster.

STEP 23
ADD axle82 3707 black
ADD bush3 6538c darkbluegray
CONNECT bush3.? -> axle82.axle1~ TURNS
WHY Threads a reinforced 8-tooth gear with its drive axle through a brace plate.

STEP 24
ADD hub45 55615 ltbluegray
ADD pin13 2780 black
CONNECT hub45.pin1 -> hub22.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin13.pin1 -> hub45.hole1~ STIFF
WHY Adds a four-way hub and a pin to brace the next shaft.

STEP 25
ADD gear169 94925 ltbluegray
ADD plate6 60483 darkbluegray
CONNECT gear169.axlehole1 -> axle82.axle2 LOCKED
WHY Adds a gear and a brace plate to the output row.

STEP 26
ADD pin14 2780 black
ADD hub12 15100 black
CONNECT pin14.pin1 -> plate6.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT hub12.pin1 -> plate6.hole1~ STIFF
WHY Pins the frame and adds a single-pin hub for the output shaft's bearing.

STEP 27
ADD ring2 18947 darkbluegray
ADD gear82 10928 darkbluegray
CONNECT ring2.? -> axle82.axle3~ TURNS
CONNECT gear82.axlehole1 -> axle82.axle4 LOCKED
WHY Adds the driving ring and the matching reinforced gear for the sequential shift.

STEP 28
ADD axle52 32073 ltbluegray
ADD crown2 3648 darkbluegray
CONNECT crown2.? -> axle52.axle1~ TURNS
WHY Adds a short axle and the last crown-style spacer onto the stepper cluster.

STEP 29
ADD pin15 2780 black
ADD plate7 60483 darkbluegray
CONNECT pin15.pin1 -> hub12.hole1~ STIFF
WHY Pins and braces the frame around the finished gear cluster.

STEP 30
ADD pin16 2780 black
ADD hub46 55615 ltbluegray
CONNECT pin16.pin1 -> plate7.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT hub46.pin1 -> plate7.hole1~ STIFF
WHY Pins the frame and adds a four-way hub for the next bearing point.

STEP 31
ADD frame2 64179 ltbluegray
ADD plate8 60483 darkbluegray
WHY Fits the second box frame and braces it with a plate, closing the far end of the gearbox.

STEP 32
ADD pin17 2780 black
ADD bush4 6538c darkbluegray
CONNECT pin17.pin1 -> plate8.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT bush4.? -> axle52.axle2~ TURNS
WHY Pins the frame and threads another spacer bush onto the output shaft.

STEP 33
ADD hub23 87082 ltbluegray
ADD axle63 3706 black
CONNECT hub23.pin1 -> plate8.hole1~ STIFF
WHY Adds a hub coupler and locks the last short axle for the stepper fork.

STEP 34
ADD bevel3 32270 black
ADD axle33 4519 ltbluegray
CONNECT bevel3.axlehole1 -> axle63.axle1 LOCKED
WHY Locks the last bevel gear and short axle pair into the stepper cluster.

STEP 35
ADD axle83 3707 black
WHY Adds the last gear axle to finish the gear row.

STEP 36
ADD bush5 6538c darkbluegray
ADD axle53 32073 ltbluegray
ADD hub24 87082 ltbluegray
CONNECT bush5.? -> axle83.axle1~ TURNS
CONNECT hub24.pin1 -> hub23.hole1~ STIFF
WHY Finishes the stepper cluster: the last spacer bush, short axle and hub coupler form the shift fork.

STEP 37
ADD axle64 3706 black
WHY Adds the last gear axle, completing every ratio pair in the stack.

STEP 38
WHY Important: check every shaft spins freely by hand before closing the box - nothing should bind.

STEP 39
WHY Closes the gearbox: all four gear pairs are in place and the stepper fork can slide the drive between them.
